<%# A field and everything that belongs to that field alone: label and input in the
    block, and what hangs off it — the text a model quoted as its source, chips that
    fill it, a hint for typing it — as `attached`, one renderable or a list of them.
    Blank entries drop out, so a caller may pass a render that produced nothing. The
    indent and the rhythm that bind them upward are .field-group in application.css. %>
<%# locals: (attached: nil) %>
<% attachments = Array(attached).select(&:present?) %>
<div class="field-group">
  <%= yield %>
  <% if attachments.any? %>
    <div class="field-group__attached"><%= safe_join(attachments) %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
